                  %mi W
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W G
            is made fairly explicit in (
            %a{:href => "#Duskin"}> Duskin, p. 85
            ).
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              The morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %mover
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W G \to \bar W G
              is a Kan fibration resolution of the point inclusion
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo →
                      %mover
                        %mi W
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {*} \to \bar W G
          %p
            This follows directly from the characterization of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
